WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.383 --> 00:00:03.824
- Effort is between you and you.

00:00:03.824 --> 00:00:05.305
There's no limits.

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:07.212
Don't let the world
ever put limits on you.

00:00:07.212 --> 00:00:09.717
Don't move to next year too fast.

00:00:09.717 --> 00:00:11.425
Just like don't go to tomorrow too fast.

00:00:11.425 --> 00:00:15.141
To the King he said King
I can't fight your fight.

00:00:15.141 --> 00:00:16.441
I got to fight my fight.

00:00:16.441 --> 00:00:20.047
I was so pissed off I said I got it.

00:00:20.047 --> 00:00:21.187
I said I got it.

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:24.075
Time slows down for no man.

00:00:24.075 --> 00:00:26.614
So the question is how
much time you gon' waste?

00:00:26.614 --> 00:00:29.163
I don't need to give
you everything you want,

00:00:29.163 --> 00:00:32.045
I just got to make sure you
have everything you need.

00:00:32.045 --> 00:00:33.962
Write down your vision.

00:00:34.858 --> 00:00:37.527
Let your subconscious
mind be the leader of you.

00:00:37.527 --> 00:00:39.028
Every footstep that's ever tooken

00:00:39.028 --> 00:00:41.749
while you been on this
earth is accounted for.

00:00:41.749 --> 00:00:45.218
Boy we are finna play a
football game tonight boys.

00:00:45.218 --> 00:00:47.284
It's gon' be a great night tonight!

00:00:47.284 --> 00:00:49.709
- He's a former American
football player who played

00:00:49.709 --> 00:00:53.691
his entire 17 year career
with the Baltimore Ravens.

00:00:53.691 --> 00:00:56.767
- He was selected to 13 Pro Bowls.

00:00:56.767 --> 00:00:59.339
- Playing middle linebacker
his entire career he's

00:00:59.339 --> 00:01:02.531
considered one of the greatest
of all time at his position.

00:01:02.531 --> 00:01:07.174
- He's Ray Lewis and here are
his top 10 rules for success.

00:01:07.174 --> 00:01:10.316
(swooshing)

00:01:10.316 --> 00:01:12.983
- Effort is between you and you.

00:01:16.985 --> 00:01:19.177
This ain't about x's and o's.

00:01:19.177 --> 00:01:22.391
Because long as you play this
game you gon' have mess ups,

00:01:22.391 --> 00:01:23.639
you gon' have great plays,

00:01:23.639 --> 00:01:24.746
you gon' have good days,

00:01:24.746 --> 00:01:26.654
you gon' have bad days.

00:01:26.654 --> 00:01:29.783
That's just the irony of this sport.

00:01:29.783 --> 00:01:32.164
But when you talk about effort,

00:01:32.164 --> 00:01:34.163
I wondered when I got to
the University of Miami

00:01:34.163 --> 00:01:36.674
because it's so many great athletes,

00:01:36.674 --> 00:01:38.009
like in this building,

00:01:38.009 --> 00:01:40.600
athlete after athlete after
athlete after athlete,

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.248
what makes me different?

00:01:42.248 --> 00:01:43.831
How do I stand out?

00:01:45.183 --> 00:01:48.490
What makes the coaches notice me?

00:01:48.490 --> 00:01:50.597
And I started figuring
out playing with the Sapps

00:01:50.597 --> 00:01:52.222
and playing all these different people,

00:01:52.222 --> 00:01:54.819
somethin' got to click in.

00:01:54.819 --> 00:01:57.456
That every time the
coach turn on the film,

00:01:57.456 --> 00:02:00.391
why is he calling my name?

00:02:00.391 --> 00:02:02.060
Why does he notice me?

00:02:02.060 --> 00:02:03.718
I ain't the fastest.

00:02:03.718 --> 00:02:05.284
I ain't the biggest.

00:02:05.284 --> 00:02:06.601
I ain't the strongest.

00:02:06.601 --> 00:02:07.934
Never have been.

00:02:10.368 --> 00:02:12.495
But Lord be my witness,

00:02:12.495 --> 00:02:14.832
I've never met a man in my life

00:02:14.832 --> 00:02:16.452
that'll flat out out work me.

00:02:16.452 --> 00:02:18.304
Honestly there's no difference.

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:19.137
The way you win it,

00:02:19.137 --> 00:02:21.065
the way I win at the game,

00:02:21.065 --> 00:02:24.061
I go at business as hard
as I went at the game.

00:02:24.061 --> 00:02:26.965
I studied businesses and I studied people

00:02:26.965 --> 00:02:30.839
as much as I studied people
trying to figure out plays.

00:02:30.839 --> 00:02:33.367
It's something I told the kids yesterday.

00:02:33.367 --> 00:02:35.556
When you see transition
really start to happen,

00:02:35.556 --> 00:02:37.464
when you really want to
transition into something,

00:02:37.464 --> 00:02:40.347
master it there's no limits.

00:02:40.347 --> 00:02:42.498
Don't let the world
ever put limits on you.

00:02:42.498 --> 00:02:44.513
You can do anything you
want to do but make sure,

00:02:44.513 --> 00:02:45.448
if you have a vision,

00:02:45.448 --> 00:02:47.213
make sure the vision is written.

00:02:47.213 --> 00:02:49.678
Make sure you have
something to actually chase

00:02:49.678 --> 00:02:51.586
and not just hoping and wishing

00:02:51.586 --> 00:02:53.967
and all these different things.

00:02:53.967 --> 00:02:55.964
I tell guys this all the time,

00:02:55.964 --> 00:02:57.869
put your plan together

00:02:57.869 --> 00:02:59.804
and then work the plan.

00:02:59.804 --> 00:03:01.624
Don't work somebody else's plan.

00:03:01.624 --> 00:03:02.457
That's one thing about the league.

00:03:02.457 --> 00:03:03.469
I love the league,

00:03:03.469 --> 00:03:05.773
but the league is somebody else's brand.

00:03:05.773 --> 00:03:07.523
You have to create your own brand yourself

00:03:07.523 --> 00:03:09.605
and your brand is whatever
you feel like doing.

00:03:09.605 --> 00:03:14.130
Whatever your heart is
passionate about chase it.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:15.963
I've had seasons where

00:03:17.885 --> 00:03:20.718
I've had the worse surgeries ever.

00:03:21.616 --> 00:03:23.366
I had seven surgeries

00:03:24.357 --> 00:03:26.252
and that alone,

00:03:26.252 --> 00:03:29.416
you ask yourself time and time
again how do you bounce back

00:03:29.416 --> 00:03:31.315
from that year in and year out?

00:03:31.315 --> 00:03:33.183
But I've always used it as

00:03:33.183 --> 00:03:35.331
taking that time to strengthen myself.

00:03:35.331 --> 00:03:37.908
I never knew I was going to play 17 years.

00:03:37.908 --> 00:03:39.548
Who could of ever thought that?

00:03:39.548 --> 00:03:40.381
You don't say,

00:03:40.381 --> 00:03:41.215
when you come into the league,

00:03:41.215 --> 00:03:42.048
you don't say you know what

00:03:42.048 --> 00:03:43.527
I'ma play 17 years.

00:03:43.527 --> 00:03:44.633
You don't even think of it that way

00:03:44.633 --> 00:03:46.819
you just say I take it year by year

00:03:46.819 --> 00:03:49.052
and that's what I try to tell kids,

00:03:49.052 --> 00:03:51.487
don't move to next year too fast.

00:03:51.487 --> 00:03:53.371
Just like don't go to tomorrow too fast.

00:03:53.371 --> 00:03:54.412
Deal with today.

00:03:54.412 --> 00:03:55.545
Deal with right now.

00:03:55.545 --> 00:03:57.474
We'd be in the locker room and
we at practice and I'm like,

00:03:57.474 --> 00:03:59.660
listen put the phones down

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:01.486
'cause these moments gon' go too fast

00:04:01.486 --> 00:04:03.748
and when they gone they gone.

00:04:03.748 --> 00:04:07.244
Before you look up you in
two three five seven 10 12

00:04:07.244 --> 00:04:08.887
if you make it that long

00:04:08.887 --> 00:04:10.326
because most of them don't.

00:04:10.326 --> 00:04:11.811
Just like you spoke about earlier,

00:04:11.811 --> 00:04:14.601
most of these young babies
never see five years.

00:04:14.601 --> 00:04:15.811
Never see seven years

00:04:15.811 --> 00:04:18.091
nevertheless a 10 year career.

00:04:18.091 --> 00:04:21.449
You try to prepare them to
understand what the moment

00:04:21.449 --> 00:04:24.446
actually feels like and
that's why I think honestly

00:04:24.446 --> 00:04:25.708
why my career lasted so long

00:04:25.708 --> 00:04:28.363
'cause I always lived in the moment.

00:04:28.363 --> 00:04:30.170
Nothing else mattered to me

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:32.002
and I was selfish at times because,

00:04:32.002 --> 00:04:33.647
even towards my family,

00:04:33.647 --> 00:04:36.600
nothing else mattered
when it came to that.

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:39.704
When it came to that I was dialed in.

00:04:39.704 --> 00:04:43.382
It's a heck of a blessing to be here now.

00:04:43.382 --> 00:04:45.382
I'm walking I'm healthy.

00:04:46.865 --> 00:04:48.948
- Still making an impact.

00:04:51.315 --> 00:04:53.589
- I just tell people I don't know how long

00:04:53.589 --> 00:04:57.143
whoever's going to play but I
will say enjoy every moment.

00:04:57.143 --> 00:04:58.670
Don't rush too fast.

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:00.636
Let your years take care of your years but

00:05:00.636 --> 00:05:01.469
go year by year,

00:05:01.469 --> 00:05:02.302
go day by day,

00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:03.135
go hour by hour,

00:05:03.135 --> 00:05:04.093
go minute by minute.

00:05:04.093 --> 00:05:05.822
If you ever research something

00:05:05.822 --> 00:05:08.041
I want everybody to do one favor,

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:11.606
I want you to research the
story of David and Goliath.

00:05:11.606 --> 00:05:13.316
I want you to understand
what the King told David

00:05:13.316 --> 00:05:16.189
when he put on the armor
on David and he said

00:05:16.189 --> 00:05:18.163
I want you to fight
Goliath with this armor

00:05:18.163 --> 00:05:18.996
because he's huge.

00:05:18.996 --> 00:05:20.339
He's nine foot tall!

00:05:20.339 --> 00:05:23.291
And David said something
that was very key to the King

00:05:23.291 --> 00:05:26.525
he said King I can't fight your fight.

00:05:26.525 --> 00:05:28.525
I got to fight my fight.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:32.170
It's about fighting our fight!

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:35.842
2005 I had one of the
most tragic injuries ever

00:05:35.842 --> 00:05:37.896
and I couldn't help my team.

00:05:37.896 --> 00:05:40.958
The leader was took away
so there could be doubt

00:05:40.958 --> 00:05:43.426
but what if you still have a leader

00:05:43.426 --> 00:05:46.196
in Joe Flacco you got to rally around him!

00:05:46.196 --> 00:05:47.682
You got to get behind
him and it ain't about

00:05:47.682 --> 00:05:49.665
wins or losses it's about loyalty!

00:05:49.665 --> 00:05:51.748
It's about understanding
I'ma make the play

00:05:51.748 --> 00:05:54.896
or I'ma watch the play be made.

00:05:54.896 --> 00:05:57.077
It's if I can tell my
safety you cover this

00:05:57.077 --> 00:05:59.356
'cause I'm going this time!

00:05:59.356 --> 00:06:02.625
It's a man on a man every
time you play the game!

00:06:02.625 --> 00:06:04.275
It'll never change!

00:06:04.275 --> 00:06:06.959
It's about winning one on one battles.

00:06:06.959 --> 00:06:08.781
Fight your fight!

00:06:08.781 --> 00:06:11.218
It's our fight to fight!

00:06:11.218 --> 00:06:13.922
One and six doesn't define who you are!

00:06:13.922 --> 00:06:15.829
What defines who you are is what you do

00:06:15.829 --> 00:06:18.024
when you one and six!

00:06:18.024 --> 00:06:20.111
What the man in you'll fight for!

00:06:20.111 --> 00:06:24.108
Give everything you got today
not because of the scoreboard

00:06:24.108 --> 00:06:25.731
but because when this game ends

00:06:25.731 --> 00:06:28.170
you will have a brother to call for life

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:30.454
knowing you gave everything you have.

00:06:30.454 --> 00:06:32.162
That's why you play as a Raven!

00:06:32.162 --> 00:06:34.243
That's why you fight as a Raven!

00:06:34.243 --> 00:06:36.846
That's why no matter what
nobody on the outside says,

00:06:36.846 --> 00:06:38.524
fight your fight!

00:06:38.524 --> 00:06:41.134
David found a way to fight his fight.

00:06:41.134 --> 00:06:42.551
Ravens Joe Flacco

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:45.427
lead your team.

00:06:45.427 --> 00:06:46.797
It's your fight!

00:06:46.797 --> 00:06:48.176
It's our fight.

00:06:48.176 --> 00:06:50.299
Let's see if somebody can
give them really who we are.

00:06:50.299 --> 00:06:53.641
I started training
because my father left me.

00:06:53.641 --> 00:06:56.488
The only way I can get
through the pain sometimes

00:06:56.488 --> 00:06:59.761
was just through push-ups and
sit-ups until I passed out.

00:06:59.761 --> 00:07:02.290
- [Speaker] For the next
decade Ray's father was barely

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:03.906
a part of his life.

00:07:03.906 --> 00:07:05.366
Then in 1990,

00:07:05.366 --> 00:07:07.044
his sophomore year in high school,

00:07:07.044 --> 00:07:10.272
a coach looking to
motivate Ray handed him a

00:07:10.272 --> 00:07:13.102
yearbook from 1975 that listed

00:07:13.102 --> 00:07:15.202
the school's athletic records.

00:07:15.202 --> 00:07:16.344
- When he handed me the book he said

00:07:16.344 --> 00:07:19.094
you'll know what to do with this.

00:07:20.681 --> 00:07:21.716
I looked at the first picture I said,

00:07:21.716 --> 00:07:22.809
that's my father!

00:07:22.809 --> 00:07:24.059
That's my daddy

00:07:26.495 --> 00:07:28.720
and I flipped the next page

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:30.759
and saw that his name

00:07:30.759 --> 00:07:33.342
was number one in every record.

00:07:34.812 --> 00:07:38.564
I was so pissed off I said I got it.

00:07:38.564 --> 00:07:39.897
I said I got it.

00:07:41.113 --> 00:07:44.825
I'm finna go through these
books and I will train so hard

00:07:44.825 --> 00:07:48.992
that I will never stop until
his name is erased ever.

00:07:51.721 --> 00:07:54.831
Day after day after day after day.

00:07:54.831 --> 00:07:56.818
I mastered it.

00:07:56.818 --> 00:07:58.863
Every time his record would fall

00:07:58.863 --> 00:08:02.421
I would go in my garage
and I would scratch.

00:08:02.421 --> 00:08:04.892
Scratch and throw it away.

00:08:04.892 --> 00:08:07.120
Say there's one down.

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:08.604
That's one down.

00:08:08.604 --> 00:08:12.771
Making the right decisions
is a one on one battle.

00:08:14.358 --> 00:08:16.517
Whatever majority of the crowd is doing

00:08:16.517 --> 00:08:18.941
find your way doing the opposite

00:08:18.941 --> 00:08:21.215
and see nine times out of 10

00:08:21.215 --> 00:08:23.259
how right you turn out to be.

00:08:23.259 --> 00:08:25.333
How many of you,

00:08:25.333 --> 00:08:26.754
a show of hands,

00:08:26.754 --> 00:08:28.004
how many of you

00:08:29.177 --> 00:08:31.232
have found out a way

00:08:31.232 --> 00:08:33.551
to not waste time?

00:08:33.551 --> 00:08:34.718
Show of hands.

00:08:36.826 --> 00:08:38.076
So it's simple.

00:08:40.065 --> 00:08:43.128
God gives us a lot of things in life

00:08:43.128 --> 00:08:45.909
but it's a couple things He don't give us

00:08:45.909 --> 00:08:49.726
and time is something he gives nobody.

00:08:49.726 --> 00:08:50.559
That's the one thing,

00:08:50.559 --> 00:08:51.529
no matter if you looked at your watch

00:08:51.529 --> 00:08:52.388
or looked at my watch,

00:08:52.388 --> 00:08:53.221
you looked at your clock,

00:08:53.221 --> 00:08:54.054
I looked at my clock,

00:08:54.054 --> 00:08:54.887
you look at your phone,

00:08:54.887 --> 00:08:56.240
I look at my phone,

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:59.038
time slows down for no man.

00:08:59.038 --> 00:09:02.443
So the question is how
much time you gon' waste?

00:09:02.443 --> 00:09:06.110
I gave up on trying to
make money years ago.

00:09:07.279 --> 00:09:11.012
I gave up on entertaining clubs years ago.

00:09:11.012 --> 00:09:12.762
14 years since I even

00:09:14.697 --> 00:09:17.939
thought about taking a step in anything

00:09:17.939 --> 00:09:21.821
that doesn't reflect
where I'm trying to go.

00:09:21.821 --> 00:09:23.203
That's what you got to put in your head.

00:09:23.203 --> 00:09:26.004
Every decision you make.

00:09:26.004 --> 00:09:28.583
Does this decision influence where I'm

00:09:28.583 --> 00:09:31.244
ultimately trying to go?

00:09:31.244 --> 00:09:34.926
Because if it does you
got to get rid of it.

00:09:34.926 --> 00:09:38.486
These conversations that
I came to have today,

00:09:38.486 --> 00:09:42.653
I can go all day 'cause I
love sharing the reason why

00:09:44.461 --> 00:09:47.691
people don't realize
what you got to give up

00:09:47.691 --> 00:09:49.024
to become great.

00:09:50.982 --> 00:09:54.899
What sacrifices you got
to make to become great.

00:09:56.934 --> 00:10:00.039
What promises you got to make to yourself

00:10:00.039 --> 00:10:01.372
to become great.

00:10:03.798 --> 00:10:06.204
Grievance ain't a thought process.

00:10:06.204 --> 00:10:08.287
Grievance is a lifestyle.

00:10:09.517 --> 00:10:11.264
It's what you live like.

00:10:11.264 --> 00:10:13.285
It's what you get every day breathing.

00:10:13.285 --> 00:10:17.451
- Why is it important
for you to give back?

00:10:17.451 --> 00:10:19.768
- It's not a secret.

00:10:19.768 --> 00:10:21.956
We didn't have much

00:10:21.956 --> 00:10:24.529
but she showed me a model

00:10:24.529 --> 00:10:27.548
and I've vowed to follow that model

00:10:27.548 --> 00:10:28.965
and that model is

00:10:30.081 --> 00:10:32.871
I don't need to give
you everything you want

00:10:32.871 --> 00:10:36.652
I have to make sure you
have everything you need.

00:10:36.652 --> 00:10:39.953
My mom gave more to
people when we didn't have

00:10:39.953 --> 00:10:43.261
and all she did was give
give give give give.

00:10:43.261 --> 00:10:46.706
I'm telling you we were
completely broke growing up

00:10:46.706 --> 00:10:48.785
and to see her giving,

00:10:48.785 --> 00:10:50.522
to see what she was built from.

00:10:50.522 --> 00:10:52.792
- In that state she still was a giver.

00:10:52.792 --> 00:10:54.262
So she was your model
right from the start.

00:10:54.262 --> 00:10:56.108
- From the start.

00:10:56.108 --> 00:10:58.262
I've had a lot of people that I admire

00:10:58.262 --> 00:11:00.920
but my greatest role model
on this earth is my mom

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:05.861
because what she taught me
no man could ever give me.

00:11:05.861 --> 00:11:07.778
Don't ever stop giving.

00:11:08.758 --> 00:11:10.455
The Good Book says giving
to the poor is like

00:11:10.455 --> 00:11:12.414
lending to God Himself.

00:11:12.414 --> 00:11:14.519
When you start to understand the Scripture

00:11:14.519 --> 00:11:16.811
and you start to really
add it to your life,

00:11:16.811 --> 00:11:18.193
it becomes a purpose.

00:11:18.193 --> 00:11:20.376
So my purpose of giving became a purpose

00:11:20.376 --> 00:11:21.676
the rest of my life

00:11:21.676 --> 00:11:23.876
to figure out different ways to give.

00:11:23.876 --> 00:11:24.709
Different ways to help.

00:11:24.709 --> 00:11:25.785
Different ways to encourage.

00:11:25.785 --> 00:11:28.835
Different ways to speak life into people.

00:11:28.835 --> 00:11:31.664
That's when my whole vision
starts to open up and say

00:11:31.664 --> 00:11:33.128
wow you know what?

00:11:33.128 --> 00:11:37.006
The game was great but the
game is actually a platform

00:11:37.006 --> 00:11:40.053
for me to really be able to
use what God has given me

00:11:40.053 --> 00:11:41.897
which is my ability to give.

00:11:41.897 --> 00:11:45.833
My infrastructure on what
I wanted to see myself,

00:11:45.833 --> 00:11:48.896
I write everything down
and I see everything.

00:11:48.896 --> 00:11:52.532
I got books and books and books from years

00:11:52.532 --> 00:11:54.405
that now I go back and
pull out and I'm like,

00:11:54.405 --> 00:11:56.488
wow you said this in '09!

00:11:57.881 --> 00:12:00.513
And now you're living it.

00:12:00.513 --> 00:12:03.444
- You wrote the vision
and you make it plain.

00:12:03.444 --> 00:12:04.861
- And you see it.

00:12:05.714 --> 00:12:07.044
That's one thing that I share with guys.

00:12:07.044 --> 00:12:08.050
I'm like listen,

00:12:08.050 --> 00:12:09.967
write down your vision.

00:12:11.035 --> 00:12:13.616
Let your subconscious
mind be the leader of you

00:12:13.616 --> 00:12:14.449
you know what I'm saying?

00:12:14.449 --> 00:12:16.278
Trust it because what you think in your

00:12:16.278 --> 00:12:19.986
subconscious mind ultimately
what your going to live.

00:12:19.986 --> 00:12:21.553
That's when God says write the vision.

00:12:21.553 --> 00:12:23.304
He said make it plain.

00:12:23.304 --> 00:12:25.757
He didn't say write a
5 thousand word essay.

00:12:25.757 --> 00:12:27.159
He just said write it.

00:12:27.159 --> 00:12:28.592
Make it plain so you can see it.

00:12:28.592 --> 00:12:31.197
So you can visually see
where you want to go

00:12:31.197 --> 00:12:32.617
on your next steps.

00:12:32.617 --> 00:12:35.563
For me I did that a lot and I still do it.

00:12:35.563 --> 00:12:37.896
If life was to end right now

00:12:41.352 --> 00:12:43.685
how would you be remembered?

00:12:44.713 --> 00:12:46.130
How will somebody

00:12:47.154 --> 00:12:48.487
think about you?

00:12:51.779 --> 00:12:53.772
Every foot step that's
ever tooken while you've

00:12:53.772 --> 00:12:56.783
been on this earth is accounted for

00:12:56.783 --> 00:12:59.116
and will be counted one day.

00:13:00.355 --> 00:13:04.008
We all got to face judgment day one day

00:13:04.008 --> 00:13:06.758
so I found out very early in life

00:13:08.445 --> 00:13:10.778
there are no breaks in life.

00:13:13.615 --> 00:13:16.436
My greatest pain I've ever
had in my entire life,

00:13:16.436 --> 00:13:17.853
I'm 39 years old.

00:13:18.723 --> 00:13:20.890
I'll be 40 in three weeks.

00:13:22.599 --> 00:13:24.281
For the first time in my life,

00:13:24.281 --> 00:13:25.864
33 years old 39 33,

00:13:28.625 --> 00:13:31.605
and the first time I actually

00:13:31.605 --> 00:13:34.188
had a chance to meet my father.

00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:39.425
It bothered me so much
because I used to look

00:13:39.425 --> 00:13:41.417
at myself in the mirror sometimes and say

00:13:41.417 --> 00:13:43.084
I know I'm who I am.

00:13:45.868 --> 00:13:47.868
Now the question remains

00:13:49.094 --> 00:13:51.095
on why inside of me

00:13:51.095 --> 00:13:52.428
there was a burn

00:13:53.597 --> 00:13:56.287
that has never stopped burning.

00:13:56.287 --> 00:13:59.188
There was a grind that
I made up in my mind.

00:13:59.188 --> 00:14:00.636
The first time I fell on my knees,

00:14:00.636 --> 00:14:01.817
I'll never forget it,

00:14:01.817 --> 00:14:04.788
I'm praying as I fall on my knees

00:14:04.788 --> 00:14:07.890
and I was a junior deacon
early and I fell on my knees

00:14:07.890 --> 00:14:09.990
and the first time I
heard God's voice He said,

00:14:09.990 --> 00:14:11.883
can you hear me now?

00:14:11.883 --> 00:14:15.225
But I'm asking to hear daddy's voice.

00:14:15.225 --> 00:14:18.624
Every Christmas I'm sending
Christmas's with a bag packed.

00:14:18.624 --> 00:14:22.583
I got a T-shirt in the
bag and one pair of jeans.

00:14:22.583 --> 00:14:25.255
I got a toothbrush but no toothpaste!

00:14:25.255 --> 00:14:27.798
And I'm saying daddy got to come today.

00:14:27.798 --> 00:14:30.464
Daddy got to come this Christmas.

00:14:30.464 --> 00:14:31.881
Daddy never came.

00:14:36.053 --> 00:14:39.803
I had a decision to make
at a very early age.

00:14:41.018 --> 00:14:44.950
Would I fold or would I make up my mind

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:47.033
to be remembered forever.

00:14:48.193 --> 00:14:51.776
I made up my mind to
be remembered forever.

00:14:54.719 --> 00:14:55.552
I did it.

00:14:57.721 --> 00:14:59.492
And you know what I did?

00:14:59.492 --> 00:15:00.825
I did it my way.

00:15:04.529 --> 00:15:06.862
And today I need a young man

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:09.522
to change their attitude

00:15:09.522 --> 00:15:12.467
of life and do it their way.

00:15:12.467 --> 00:15:15.967
There is somebody sitting in this audience

00:15:17.569 --> 00:15:19.652
that has one thing to do.

00:15:21.075 --> 00:15:23.796
The moment you leave here

00:15:23.796 --> 00:15:28.174
make up in your mind that
I'm a different person.

00:15:28.174 --> 00:15:31.140
Make up in your mind
that there is something

00:15:31.140 --> 00:15:32.807
way greater than me.

00:15:34.755 --> 00:15:36.953
Everybody in this room,

00:15:36.953 --> 00:15:40.913
this day can have a real
change on somebody's life

00:15:40.913 --> 00:15:43.746
by the way you live your own life.

00:15:44.938 --> 00:15:46.688
No pain lasts always.

00:15:50.579 --> 00:15:52.162
I can do all things

00:15:56.876 --> 00:15:58.768
through Christ who strengthens me.

00:15:58.768 --> 00:16:01.324
- [Announcer] At middle
linebacker from Miami.

00:16:01.324 --> 00:16:02.991
Number 52 Ray Lewis.

00:16:05.282 --> 00:16:06.963
